nal data transfers are required, increasing computational cost.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'SIMULTANEOUS APPLICATION TO BOTH LAYERS': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The need to apply sparse methods to both fully connected and convolution layers simultaneously, which is a desirable feature not fully addressed by current methods.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Limited Applicability to Filter Sizes': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The challenge that some prior sparse convolution methods are only applicable to large filters, limiting their usage for modern CNNs with small filters.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Simultaneous Sparsity Application': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The challenge that current sparse CNN methods mostly focus on either fully connected layers or convolution layers, while it is desirable to apply sparse methods to both layers simultaneously.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Xeon processors': {'type': ['generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['A family of x86-64 microprocessors designed, manufactured, and sold by Intel.', 'The specific platform where the 3.4x speedup was achieved.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 3]}, 'Atom processors': {'type': ['generic', 'generic', 'generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['A series of x86 and x86-64 microprocessors designed and produced by Intel.', 'The specific platform where the 7.3x speedup was achieved.', 'Processors where sparse convolution outperforms dense convolution in a wider range of sparsity.', 'The specific type of processor where the performance of sparse convolution is being evaluated.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 3, 5, 5]}, 'End-to-end performance': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The overall performance of a system, from input to output.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Classification throughput': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The rate at which a system can classify images.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Speedup of convolution layers': {'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'description': ['The speedups achieved by the sparse CNN implementation, specifically 3.4x and 7.3x, compared to the best dense direct convolution performance on Xeon and Atom processors, respectively.', 'The objective of achieving speed improvements in convolution layers, as indicated by the 3.4x and 7.3x speedups.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 3]}, 'AlexNet classification throughput': {'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'description': ['The classification throughput achieved by the sparse CNN implementation, specifically 2,371 and 120 images per second on respective platforms.', 'The objective of achieving a specific classification throughput, measured in images per second, for the AlexNet model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 3]}, 'Research thrusts': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The research areas or focuses within sparse CNN research, specifically identified by the citations [19, 8, 14].'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, '2371 Images Per Second Throughput': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The classification throughput achieved on a specific platform for AlexNet.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, '120 Images Per Second Throughput': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The classification throughput achieved on a different platform for AlexNet.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'direct sparse convolution algorithm': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['An algorithm presented to advance the state-of-the-art in sparse convolution for speeding up CNNs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'SpMV': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Sparse Matrix-Vector multiplication, a computational kernel.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'speeding up CNNs': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The objective of improving the computational efficiency of CNNs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Sparse Methods': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['Refers to the specific algorithms or techniques used to create sparse representations, which are mentioned in the text for accelerating CNNs.', 'Techniques used to achieve sparsity in CNNs, mentioned in the text for accelerating CNNs.', 'The general category of techniques used to create the Holistic SparseCNN, including those applied to convolution and fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 4, 7]}, 'Holistical Optimization of Speed and Size': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The challenge of simultaneously optimizing the speed and size of sparse CNNs, specifically addressing the impact of convolution and fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Acceleration': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The objective of improving the speed of CNNs, specifically in the context of convolution layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'FLOP/s': {'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'description': ['Floating point operations per second, a metric used to measure the computational speed of convolution operations.', 'The performance metric being optimized, representing the number of floating-point operations per second. This is the metric used to compare the speed of sparse and dense convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5, 5]}, 'GEMM': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['General Matrix Multiplication, used in the implementation of fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'SpMDM': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Sparse matrix and dense matrix multiplication, a technique that can be leveraged to exploit sparsity in fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Speedup': {'type': ['generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['The performance improvement achieved by using sparse convolution compared to dense convolution.', 'The improvement in performance (e.g., FLOP/s) achieved by using sparse convolution compared to dense convolution, which is directly affected by the proportion of non-zeros in filters (sparsity).'], 'source_chunk_index': [5, 5]}, 'Weight tensor': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A multi-dimensional array of weights used in convolutional layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Lowering and lifting process': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A process that has demonstrated overhead for dense convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Bottleneck': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['A component that limits the overall performance of a system.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Speedups': {'type': ['task', 'generic'], 'description': ['The objective of achieving faster computation or improved performance, specifically in the context of sparse convolution.', 'The performance gains achieved by the Holistic SparseCNN, specifically 3.4x and 7.3x speedups of convolution layers over the best dense convolution on representative server and mobile platforms.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5, 7]}, 'Lower Bound of Useful Sparsity': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The minimum level of sparsity required for sparse convolution to provide a speedup over dense convolution. Below this threshold, sparse convolution offers no performance benefit.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'Holistic SparseCNN': {'type': ['method', 'method'], 'description': ['A method that achieves a classification speed of 2,371 images per second on BDW without accuracy drop compared to the reference Caffe model.', 'A collection of techniques designed to unleash the full potential of sparse CNNs, achieving high classification speed.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6, 7]}, 'weight decay': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A regularization technique used to prevent overfitting.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Caffe model': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A reference model used for comparison.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'BDW': {'type': ['generic', 'generic'], 'description': ['A platform or environment where the classification speed was measured.', 'The platform on which sparse convolution is slower than dense convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6, 7]}, 'regularization parameters': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Parameters used to control the regularization process.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Weight Decay 1e-5': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The weight decay parameter used in the experiment.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Weight Decay 5e-5': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Another weight decay parameter used in the experiment.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Weight Decay 6e-5': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['Another weight decay parameter used in the experiment.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'conv1': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The first convolutional layer in AlexNet.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'conv2': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The second convolutional layer in AlexNet.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Weight decay values': {'type': ['generic'], 'description': ['The specific values used for weight decay, which are 1e-5, 5e-5, and 6e-5.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'classification accuracy': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The objective of improving the accuracy of classification tasks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'SGEMM': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Highly optimized performance used as a proxy of dense convolution performance to quantify layer-wise speedups.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'dense CNN implementation': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A CNN implementation where all conv and fc layers would perform at the speed of SGEMM.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Size': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ["The objective of reducing the model's size, in addition to speed and accuracy, as a goal of the Holistic SparseCNN."], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'Inference speed': {'description': ['The speed at which a model can make predictions or draw conclusions.'], 'type': ['method', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Sparsity': {'description': ['The proportion of zero-valued elements in a tensor or matrix, often used in the context of neural networks.', 'A technique used in CNNs to reduce model size and/or accelerate classification speed.', 'The proportion of zero-valued elements in a matrix or tensor, a key concept in sparse CNNs.', 'The proportion of zero-valued elements in a weight tensor, influencing the performance of sparse convolution.', 'The objective of reducing the number of parameters in a model.'], 'type': ['task', 'method', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1, 2, 5, 6]}, 'Data centers': {'description': ['Locations where CNNs are widely deployed.', 'A platform where CNN models are deployed.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 1]}, 'Fully connected layers': {'description': ['Layers in a neural network where each neuron is connected to all neurons in the previous layer.', "Layers within a Convolutional Neural Network that often contain a large proportion of the model's parameters.", 'Layers in a neural network that can become a bottleneck after sparse convolution optimizations.', 'Layers within a CNN that are fully connected.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [0, 2, 4, 5, 6, 7]}, 'Image recognition': {'description': ['The task of identifying and classifying objects within images.', 'A specific application of CNNs mentioned in the text.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Video analytics': {'description': ['The process of analyzing video data to extract meaningful information.', 'A specific application of CNNs mentioned in the text.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Autonomous driving': {'description': ['The technology and application of self-driving vehicles.', 'A specific application of CNNs mentioned in the text.'], 'type': ['task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Mobile platforms': {'description': ['Computing platforms with limited resources, such as smartphones and autonomous driving systems.', 'Representative mobile platforms where the Holistic SparseCNN was tested.', 'The platform where the 3.4x and 7.3x speedups were observed.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 7]}, 'Model size': {'description': ['The amount of memory required to store a trained machine learning model.', 'The amount of memory a model occupies.', 'The objective of minimizing the number of parameters in the model.'], 'type': ['task', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 4, 6]}, 'Accuracy': {'description': ["The degree to which a model's output matches the correct answer.", 'The requirement for the CNN model to correctly classify inputs.', "The objective of achieving a high degree of correctness in the model's predictions."], 'type': ['task', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 6]}, 'Speed': {'description': ['The rate at which a model can process data and produce results.', 'The requirement for the CNN model to perform classifications quickly.', 'The objective of increasing the speed of the CNNs.'], 'type': ['task', 'generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 7]}, 'Model Size': {'description': ['The requirement for the CNN model to have a small memory footprint.', 'The amount of memory a model occupies.', 'The objective of minimizing the number of parameters in the model.'], 'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 4, 6]}, 'Sparse CNN': {'description': ['A type of Convolutional Neural Network that aims to reduce model size and improve classification speed by sparsifying or compressing layers.', 'A CNN implementation designed to reduce model size and accelerate classification speed.', 'Convolutional Neural Networks that utilize sparsity to improve performance.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 7]}, 'Convolution layers': {'description': ['Layers within a Convolutional Neural Network responsible for the majority of the computation (FLOPS).', 'Layers within a CNN that perform convolution operations.', 'Layers in a neural network where a bulk of computation occurs.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]}, 'Classification speed': {'description': ['The objective of improving the rate at which a CNN can classify inputs.', 'The speed at which a model can classify images.', 'The speed at which the Holistic SparseCNN performs classification, measured as 120 images per second.'], 'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 7]}, 'Sparse convolution': {'description': ['A technique used in sparse CNNs to reduce computational requirements by applying sparsity to convolution operations.', 'A technique used to reduce the computational cost of convolution operations.', 'A convolutional technique that exploits sparsity in the weight tensor to potentially achieve speedups over dense convolution.', 'A method to speed up CNNs by reducing redundant computations.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 3, 4, 5]}, 'Arithmetic intensity': {'description': ['A measure of the ratio of computation to data movement, relevant to the efficiency of sparse convolution.', 'A measure of the ratio of computation to memory access.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Sparse Convolution': {'description': ['A method used to reduce compute requirements in CNNs by applying sparsity to convolution layers.', 'A specific technique that leverages sparsity to speed up CNNs.', 'A method to speed up CNNs by reducing redundant computations.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [2, 4]}, 'Lower Arithmetic Intensity': {'description': ['A challenge of sparse convolution, referring to the reduced efficiency of arithmetic operations, leading to increased data transfer overhead.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Limitation to Large Filters': {'description': ['A challenge where some sparse convolution methods are only applicable to large filters (e.g., 9x9), limiting their use in modern CNNs with small filters (e.g., 3x3).'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, '3.4x Speedup': {'description': ['The speedup achieved on Xeon processors for convolution layers in AlexNet.', 'The specific speedup value observed for convolution layers.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 7]}, '7.3x Speedup': {'description': ['The speedup achieved on Atom processors for convolution layers in AlexNet.', 'The specific speedup value observed for convolution layers.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 7]}, 'classification speed': {'description': ['The speed at which a model can classify data.', 'The objective of optimizing the speed at which the model classifies images.', 'The objective of increasing the speed of classification.', 'The speed at which the Holistic SparseCNN performs classification, measured as 120 images per second.'], 'type': ['generic', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 6, 7]}, 'dense convolution': {'description': ['Standard convolution operation without sparsity.', 'A standard convolutional technique used as a baseline for comparison with sparse convolution.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 5]}, 'FC decay multiplier 1': {'description': ['The specific value used for the FC decay multiplier, which is 1.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'FC decay multiplier 0.1': {'description': ['The specific value used for the FC decay multiplier, which is 0.1.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'cross-layer holistic methodology': {'description': ['A methodology that exploits the synergies of sparse methods on convolution layers and fully connected layers.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'server platforms': {'description': ['Representative server platforms where the Holistic SparseCNN was tested.', 'The platform where the 3.4x speedup was observed.'], 'type': ['generic'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}}
